    "assumptions": [
        "The default and the geometry checks above are the v2 side_tab in its own frame: the +X-side tab centred on its M4 station (Y = 0). Four of them on a deck are MEAN WELL's own bracket pattern; the fit block places them on both stations and both sides and drops the vendor solid in.",
        "HORIZONTAL (bottom face down) is the only attitude the NSP-1600 datasheet qualifies: its derating curve is labelled (HORIZONTAL) and no other is published. Every kit here holds the unit in that attitude.",
        "Every hole position comes from the vendor B-rep translated by (-66.787, -354.15, -1.5) - a pure translation, so no mirror is possible - and agrees with the Case No. 296A drawing to 0.002 mm. Thread sizes, the 4 mm / 5 mm penetration limits and torques are datasheet figures; the STEP carries no thread.",
        "The fan-end pair of side M4s (Y = -257.8) is NOT modelled as a thread in the vendor STEP - each wall shows a dia 5.0 clearance opening with nothing behind it. The datasheet promises M4 there and the vendor's own four-tab kit depends on it, as the deck tab kit does. Verify with a screw on a real unit before relying on the deck tab kit; the deck can also be drilled for the three bottom M3 as insurance.",
        "The tab lies flush on the side wall because its foot bends OUTWARD, putting the bend fillet outside the unit's corner; fit_check.py measures the leg's bearing area by pressing the unit sideways into the tabs. The v1 channels bend their walls up from under the unit, which is why they need the 3 mm gap and the spacer ring.",
        "The terminal box has a floor and closed cable exits so it is finger-safe with nothing under it. Its fixed openings are 5 mm louvres and a 6 mm LED window; the dia 18 / dia 12 exits and the harness slot are cable-filled in service. Its cavity is checked from the terminal plate (Y = 0), not from the box's own 8 mm-offset edge.",
        "Design shock is 20 g on 1.8 kg = 353 N, the same figure the Bedrock family uses. The bulkhead straps' stiffness estimate (about 70 Hz first mode with the unit on them) is reasoned from a cantilever-strip model, not measured; a 12 mm lip is the recorded upgrade if a rig test finds it.",
        "K-factor 0.42 is assumed, not measured. It affects only the developed flat patterns.",
        "cylinder_at points lie on a feature's axis. Countersinks are cones and are not covered by cylinder checks; their arithmetic is enforced in code."
    ],
    "unresolved": []
